  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "\"~ (increased/reduced) to: {0}\" format string, which is unnatural when {0} contains a non-numeric string.\n\nIn fact, 24823,24821,24803,24801,24799,24797 use that format and insert a numeric value in {0}. (\"{0} MB\", \"X{0}\").\n\nHowever, non-numeric strings (\"Disabled\", \"No Limit\") are sometimes inserted, and it seems a bit odd to use \"increased/reduced\" for them.\n\nTherefore, we would like to have a string for when a non-numeric string is inserted.",
